## Third-Party Component: Zoobot Encoder (GPL-3.0)

**WARNING — GPL-3.0 "Copyleft" Component**

The file `models/zoobot_encoder_greyscale.onnx` (57.1 MB) contains pretrained
weights derived from Zoobot (https://github.com/mwalmsley/zoobot), which is
licensed under the **GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)**.

### GPL-3.0 Compliance Impact

The GPL-3.0 is a strong copyleft license. If you **distribute** (as defined
by the GPL) any Docker image or software package containing this file, you
MUST also make the **complete corresponding source code** of the entire
platform available under GPL-3.0-compatible terms.

### What "Distribution" Means

- ✅ **Internal use only** (private servers, local Docker instances accessible
  only by your organization) — does NOT trigger GPL source disclosure.
- ⚠️ **Docker image pushed to a public registry** (Docker Hub, GitHub
  Container Registry, etc.) — TRIGGERS GPL source disclosure obligation.
- ⚠️ **Deployment to a public-facing server** accessible by users outside
  your organization — may trigger GPL obligations depending on jurisdiction.
  Consult legal counsel.
- ⚠️ **Sharing Docker images with external collaborators** — TRIGGERS GPL
  source disclosure obligation.

### Recommended Actions

1. **Immediate (no cost)**: Add a build-time flag to optionally exclude
   `zoobot_encoder_greyscale.onnx` from the Docker image. When excluded,
   the lightweight classifier still works (at reduced accuracy ~40-60%).

2. **Short-term**: Contact Zoobot author Mike Walmsley for a written
   licensing exception for academic/non-commercial use.

3. **Medium-term**: Train a replacement encoder on public-domain survey data
   (e.g., DECaLS DR9) under MIT or Apache 2.0 license.

4. **If distributing publicly**: Prepare the complete platform source code
   for GPL-3.0 release, or remove the Zoobot-derived weights before
   distribution.

### Current Status (2026-07-26)

- [ ] GPL compliance plan not formalized
- [ ] No written exemption from Zoobot author
- [ ] No build flag to exclude GPL model
- [ ] No replacement encoder trained under permissive license
- [x] License documented in model metadata
- [x] License noted in dl_inference.py source code

